# Belt-and-suspenders. The real fix for shipping the WASM is enumerating the
# pkg/ files EXPLICITLY in package.json "files" — npm's packlist otherwise
# excludes the whole pkg/ directory because it contains its own package.json
# (wasm-pack --target bundler output), which npm (esp. node20/npm10 in CI)
# treats as a nested-package boundary and skips. Listing each pkg file by path
# bypasses that. This file's presence also stops npm consulting the repo
# .gitignore (which ignores packages/*/pkg/). See rust-skyfire#76. Excludes
# nothing itself — "files" governs the tarball.
